# Agave (Parry's agave): a dense, FLOWER-SHAPED rosette (~1-2 m across) of many broad, short, cupped grey-green leaves
# in overlapping rings, every leaf curving IN toward the centre like a petal (`Cup`), the outer ones spreading, the inner
# ones closing into a bud, each widest near its middle and ending in a point. It grows ON ITS OWN in the hot desert (its
# Placement block: no tree needed); Climate Desert - no tree's - so it is never a tree's undergrowth.
# The leaves are the modules: one blade each (`Section`: wide, thin, a gutter on top; `Swell`: widest near the middle;
# `Tip`: a closed point), no leaf cards. The crown starts above the ground on a short hidden trunk: the outer leaves
# rise off it.
TreeSpecies Agave
	Kind Bush
	Climate Desert
	Seed 151
	Scale 1.0 1.6
	Wind
		Trunk 0
		Branch 0.05
	Trunk
		Count 2
		Height 0.3 0.4
		Radius 0.1
		Taper 0.7
		Flare 0
		Sink 0.1
		Curve 2
		Rings 3
		Sides 8
	Crown
		Shape Cone
		Start 0.3
		Radius 0.65
		Slots 40
		Fill 1
		Angle 70 5
		AngleVar 5
		BranchRadius 3
	# 3 leaf modules (3 widths, `Section` widthVar): each one is a billboard bake and a row of the card atlas.
	Module
		Count 3
		Radius 0.11
		Curve 6 3
		UpAttract 0.1
		Cup 50
		Rings 14
		Sides 12
		Section 1.8 0.3 0.6 0.25
		Swell 1.0
		Tip 0.25
	Leaves
		Type Single
		PerBranch 0
	# Two baked plants are enough (they look alike): half the billboard textures.
	Bake
		Variants 2
	Billboard
		Distance 25
		Resolution 256
		FadeWidth 6
	Bark
		Plates 8 1
		Crack 0.03
		Breakup 0.95
		Relief 0.15
		Lichen 0
	Color
		Bark 0.46 0.60 0.49
		Leaf 0.46 0.60 0.49
	Placement
		Density 30
		Temperature 20 1000
		Precipitation 40 350
		ClimateWidth 0.02
		Cluster 50 0.5
		MaxSlope 0.9
